  "summary": "An oil-sealed rotary vane vacuum pump draws gas from a vessel by trapping it between vanes in an eccentric chamber, compressing it to just above atmospheric pressure and expelling it through an oil-covered exhaust valve. The oil seals the small clearances, which lets these pumps reach a rough to medium vacuum (typically down to ~0.1 mbar or below for two-stage designs).",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive-displacement vacuum pump",
    "type": "Oil-sealed rotary vane, single stage"
  },
